 "about": "The living people Producers and flagships never names: in prose, in a card, in a question or in a source's title (tools/caskhouses/schema.mjs, livingIn). A name is matched as a whole phrase, folded (accents off, case off). A house keeps its name: every label of the roster and a record's own bottlings are taken out of a sentence first, so Pappy Van Winkle, Jack Daniel's and Jim Beam are labels and never refused. Seeded on 21 November 2026 from every list this repo already held: tools/caskstyles/people.json, tools/backbar/people.json, LIVING in tools/check-producers.mjs, and the living and the workplace's people of tools/brew/people.json (its long dead, whom a house history may need, were left where they are); plan.json's notes name no living person the lists lacked. names is the living, or those not known to have died: add a name the moment a source shows one, in the same commit as the fragment, and never remove one. historic is the dead whose names would otherwise be refused, because a living person's name sits inside theirs or because an older list held them: each is taken out of a sentence before the living are looked for. A name goes on historic only with the year of death in two sources, stated in the record's report.",
